      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5227964::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interstitial carbon will increase grain-boundary cohesion in (MnNiSi)0.62(FeCoGe)0.38.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increased grain-boundary cohesion will impede crack initiation in the target alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon may promote beneficial twinning in the target alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5227964::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Carbon may produce minor nanoscale precipitation that improves toughness.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5227964::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interstitial carbon provides solid-solution strengthening in high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5227964::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interstitial carbon will increase the yield and compressive strengths of (MnNiSi)0.62(FeCoGe)0.38.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5227964::webcard"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "An optimized carbon addition will preserve the phase balance required for the target alloy's caloric transition.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimized carbon addition will not significantly shift the caloric transition temperature.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carbon-modified alloy will show a 20–50% improvement in mechanical integrity relative to the unchanged alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carbon-modified alloy will have a reduced cracking propensity relative to the unchanged alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The carbon-modified alloy will retain its large caloric response under field and pressure cycling identical to that applied to the control.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed benefits will persist under moderate fields, pressures, temperature cycles, and mechanical loading typical of caloric operation.",
